messages.body_plain:
I don't see any reason you couldn't use hierarchical intercepts
and slopes.  We typically give those multivariate priors --- see
the manual chapter on regression.

Identifiability is important, so if it requires a sum-to-zero
constraint, you need to implement that.  I didn't understand why
you thought the method in the manual won't work.

But before trying to generalize, you want to make sure you can
fit before the generalization.  Often the problem is with
identifiability --- hierarchical models are only weakly identifiable
and often need stronger priors to control the posterior variance.

- Bob

